{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1530472546,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMzczMTQ1ODY=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2684","origin":"github"},"title":"More flexible substitutions for `run`","message":"So far we have been adding supported place holders one by one. However, I think we need more and we shouldnt implement them ourselves. Current use case:\n\nI need to provide license info to a command call that is different depending on where the execution is happening. Ideally, there would be a way to put this info in the config, and have it be overwritten by user config if needed.\n\nThat could be achieved by something like: have a dedicated cfg namespace datalad.substituions.LABEL, where LABEL can be any valid config name and can be used in any  call like {LABEL}. Run would simple take this namespace and pass it on for string formating.\n\nWhat do you think?","files":null}]}